# config/vpn/exclude.list
#
# Applications that should bypass the Mullvad VPN tunnel via
# split-tunneling.  scripts/vpn-exclude.sh reads this file, finds each
# binary on PATH, and generates a wrapper at
#     ~/.local/bin/vpn-excluded/<app>
# that exec's `mullvad-exclude <real-binary> "$@"`.  The shim dir is
# prepended to PATH by ~/.zshrc so the shim is what gets invoked when
# you type the app name in a shell.
#
# Per-machine override:
#     ~/.config/dotfiles-local/vpn-exclude.list
# If that file exists, it REPLACES this one entirely (mirrors the rest
# of the dotfiles-local override pattern).  Use it when one machine
# needs a different exclusion set without diverging the repo.
#
# CLI:
#     scripts/vpn-exclude.sh add <app>     — append to whichever file is active
#     scripts/vpn-exclude.sh remove <app>  — drop from whichever file is active
#     scripts/vpn-exclude.sh list          — show effective set + shim status
#     scripts/vpn-exclude.sh apply         — regenerate shims (idempotent)
#     scripts/vpn-exclude.sh status        — mullvad daemon + shim dir health
#
# Syntax:
#   • One application name per line.
#   • Lines starting with `#` are comments.
#   • Empty lines are ignored.
#   • Whitespace around names is stripped.
#   • App names must be plain (no slashes, ≤ 64 chars, [A-Za-z0-9._-] only).
#
# Trust note:
#   The `mullvad-exclude` binary is provided by `mullvad-vpn` (Tier 1).
#   Without it the shim degrades to running the bare command — same as
#   if no VPN were active.  No traffic is leaked accidentally.

# AI tools that misbehave under Mullvad's exit IPs (rate-limit triggers,
# regional content blocks, captchas).
claude
